## Summary

This pull request adds Telegram notifications for newly created borrowings.

The notification is sent to a private administrator chat and contains the borrower, book and borrowing details.

## Changes

- initialized the Notifications application;
- added environment-based Telegram bot configuration;
- added the `python-telegram-bot` dependency;
- added a reusable helper for sending messages through the Telegram Bot API;
- added formatting for new borrowing notifications;
- escaped dynamic values used in Telegram HTML messages;
- integrated notification sending with the borrowing creation endpoint;
- updated the OpenAPI description for borrowing creation;
- mocked Telegram execution in existing borrowing view tests to prevent external API requests;
- added Telegram variables to `.env.sample` without exposing private credentials.

## Notification Details

Each notification contains:

- borrower email and user ID;
- book title, author and ID;
- borrowing ID;
- borrow date and expected return date;
- remaining book inventory.

## Security

The real Telegram bot token and chat ID are stored only in the local `.env` file.

The repository contains only safe placeholder values in `.env.sample`.

## Notes

Telegram messages are sent directly during borrowing creation at this stage. Background execution will be introduced separately with Celery.
